{"name":"Greenwich","hex":"#475b49","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Greenwich","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A place in England:\nA town on the south bank of the River Thames in south-east Greater London, England, through which the prime meridian passes .\nA royal borough in Greater London, which includes the town.\nA southern suburb of Ipswich, Suffolk .\nA hamlet in Fonthill Gifford parish, Wiltshire .","A town on the south bank of the River Thames in south-east Greater London, England, through which the prime meridian passes ."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Greenwich"}],"entries":[{"title":"Greenwich","blocks":[{"text":"Greenwich is an affluent area in south-east London, England, within the Royal Borough of Greenwich and the ceremonial county of Greater London, 5.5 miles (8.9 km) east-south-east of Charing Cross. It contains the UNESCO World Heritage Site of Maritime Greenwich."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ac/312SFEC_LONDON-20070917.JPG/330px-312SFEC_LONDON-20070917.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Greenwich","wikidata":"Q179385"},{"title":"Greenwich (UK Parliament constituency)","blocks":[{"text":"Greenwich was a constituency in south-east London, which returned at first two, then one member (MP) to the House of Commons of the UK Parliament. It existed from 1832 to 1997. Elections used the first past the post system; when this elects more than one member, it is sometimes called plurality-at-large voting."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/19/United_Kingdom_general_election_1837.svg/330px-United_Kingdom_general_election_1837.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Greenwich_(UK_Parliament_constituency)","wikidata":"Q5604826"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikiped